+## 2026.11.12a
+
+**Release S, the slimming** (the maintainer's release, built in a separate clone on the owner's word of 2026-11-11 after the pace audit of 2026-11-09, its terms agreed with the bridge's supervisor on 2026-11-10; three pull requests through the full gate: the programs with their tests, the test retirements alone, the texts with this stamp): the loop sheds what cost rounds without catching defects, and nothing that caught one. The measure is the audit's: of the rounds of weeks 42 to 45, most went to wording pins, to records pull requests taking the whole gate, to whole-suite runs repeated per push and to re-reads after a compaction of text the step in hand never used. The programs that change: `bridge_env.py`, `bridge-run.py`, `cursor-agent.shim`, `bridge-check.py`, `bridge-install.py`, `completion-check.py`, `review-guard.py`, `session-start.py`, `plan-check.py` and `pace-report.py`. Against 2026.11.11a: no file new, none removed, no allow entry new (`review-guard.py premerge-records` runs on the guard's existing entry).
+
+**What changed**
+- **Wording is no longer pinned by tests** (S1): 6 size and hash pins (122 cases), 5 per-file caps (18 cases), the 34 prose-literal tests this release's text touched (42 cases) and 3 pins on a record's wording are retired, 48 functions and 185 cases of 5,289 (the list below, by file and name; approved by the owner by file and count on 2026-11-12). The register follows: R-032's sentence is revised in place (the two word budgets for the 1,500 lines and 60,000 characters per module), and where a retired test was a label's only evidence the cell names the text (R-042, R-045, R-047, R-049, R-050, R-051). Kept: the digest's cap of 9,500 characters, every value the owner chose, every line a program parses. In their place two word budgets held by `tests/test_release_s_budgets.py`: the rulebook (every `.md` under `bridge/` except this file and the design seeds) at 150,000 words, and each phase or step file at 8,000. An increment that changes instruction text alone has no wording test and no mutation run; its register row takes the text form of Evidence, `text: <file>.md :: <heading> (#<pull request>)`. The form exists only in a project whose `project.json` declares where its instruction texts are (`instruction_texts`, a list of folders, never a record folder; this repository declares `bridge/`), which is no project whose product is ordinary software: there a text entry fails. `completion-check.py` verifies each entry: the file under a declared folder, the heading outside a code block, the pull request's squash on `origin/main` and having changed that file. For a row whose sentence names a program a text entry never counts; its test stands beside it.
+- **A records-only pull request takes the short gate** (S2): `review-guard.py premerge-records [<pr>]` decides by path, type and mode and prints `SHORT GATE`, `FULL GATE` or `OK - records only`. A record is a text or a picture (`.md`, `.json`, `.txt`, `.csv`, an image) under `docs/` or `handoff/`, or `project.json`, as a plain file. The full gate stays for everything else and for the records a program reads to decide a gate: the run parameters, a build plan, the roster, everything under `docs/diagrams/` (the diagrams, their index and the deviations decide what the diagram check allows), a removed status file, inventory, register or project file, a tool's configuration under a record folder (`package.json` and its like, `tsconfig.*.json`, every `requirements*.txt`) and any hidden file or folder, the register where a Status cell changed, a row left, a new row is not `planned` or a built row changed in any cell, the inventory where a line naming the threat model or a line under a heading naming it changed (the section opens on any line that reads as that heading and ends only on a heading Markdown would draw), the project file where `instruction_texts` changed, and a pull request into another branch than `main`. The short gate is one `diff-reviewer` read, CI green and `premerge-records <n>`: no snapshot, no Review B, no mutation run, no round counted. The program checks neither CI nor the read: the branch rule holds the first, the supervisor's step the second.
+- **The late-round filter states its path** (S3): from the round the program holds, a reviewer's finding that sends work back names its class and the path by which the defect is reached, or `no path stated`; an unstated path is recorded, and a reproduction decides (rule 26).
+- **After a compaction the hook names less** (S4): the status file, the last entries of `run/supervisor/in-flight.md` and the one file of the step in hand; the policy at the merge step, a pitfall by its `### KP-` heading, the inventory by section, everything else on demand. `session-start.py` prints `on demand:` lines in place of the old list.
+- **A large increment is noted at the plan check** (S5): `plan-check.py` prints a `note:` for an increment with more than twelve acceptance items in its `Done when:` or more than twelve Scope paths; a note, never a finding.
+- **The rule budget** (S6): new instruction text retires equal text; the budget is raised only visibly, in the pull request that needs it, with the reason.
+- **One whole suite per pull request, and it is CI's** : the pre-push whole-suite run with the pull-request variables is gone; a test that reads those variables is run alone with them set (KP-074). Every other suite is the launcher's and targeted.
+- **The status file loses two lines**: `Increment:` and `Last accepted:` leave the template and this repository's own file; no program read them, git names the merged increment, and a line naming its own pull request's number in advance cost a re-review whenever another merge came first. `tests/test_release_b_bootstrap.py` now requires `In flight: none` and the absence of the two lines.
+- **A fix that regresses** : after the first regression a fix causes, the next fix brief gets one Review A read before launch, against the finding and the tests that pin the touched subsystem, which the brief names and the builder runs; after the second, a resolution round. A class line never lifts a round for a regression the previous fix caused.
