+**Running projects must**
+- *(all phases)* Install with every project paused at a merge boundary, everything committed, restart, run `/calibrate-bridge` before the next increment. The installer ends 0 with `RESULT: INSTALLED TREE MATCHES bridge 2026.11.12a` and keeps 2026.11.11a as the way back; `bridge-check.py` then reads the agent home's login link.
+- *(all phases)* The text is in force from the calibration, reopening no gate. At the calibration's checkpoint the status file loses its `Increment:` and `Last accepted:` lines, in a records-only commit; a pull request open at the install is finished under the gate it began with.
+- *(all phases)* At the calibration, one stripped suite run (`bridge-run.py --strip --kind test`, as the loop's step 4 launches it) before the next increment: a stripped run's `APPDATA` and `LOCALAPPDATA` now lead to the agent home, and a suite that needs a tool's state there (npm's global prefix, Volta, `py.ini`) fails visibly. Such a failure is reported to the maintainer, not worked around in the project.
+- *(all phases)* Changed on purpose, each named so that no one reads it as an oversight: the first fix that regresses no longer stops the loop (the next fix brief gets one Review A read; the second regression goes to a resolution round); from the first pass of a stage review only a finding of the five blocking classes opens a fix, and the stage's `Blocking class:` lift is gone with the third pass; the pitfalls are read by their headings on entering the configure and build phases, an entry when its heading or a step names it; no brief has the builder run the whole test tree, and the known-failures bullet went with that; `KP-041`'s copy back to the status file is dropped (`In flight:` stays `none`).
+- *(all phases)* A test run through the launcher is refused, with the variable's name, where the session's environment or a key file sets `PYTEST_ADDOPTS` with an option or target the launcher refuses, `PYTEST_PLUGINS`, or, for a `uv run pytest` suite, a `UV_` name outside the list above (an index address, `UV_PYTHON`). On the owner's computer none is set (read 2026-11-12). Where one is needed, report it to the maintainer: the list is extended in a release, never worked around in the project.
+- *(all phases)* A project's own tests that pin instruction wording, sizes or hashes of bridge text are retired as next touched, never in a pull request of their own; a value the owner chose and a line a program parses stay pinned (rule 52).
+- *(building)* From the next brief: the `Round cause:` line on every numbered brief after the first; the reviewer's class and path on each finding that sends work back; the short gate for a records-only pull request; the whole suite once per pull request, as CI's run.
+- *(building, change cycle)* A register row whose only evidence was a retired wording test takes the text form of Evidence at the next records commit.
+- *(all phases)* At the calibration, `completion-check.py --mode plan` (and `--mode done` on a finished project): a `built` row whose Evidence names only a document under `docs/`, `handoff/` or `run/` now fails with NO EVIDENCE, as does one whose only tracked mention is such a document. Name the row's test; where there is none, the row was never proved, which is a finding for the owner's report and never a reason to restore the document as evidence.
+- *(configuration)* A project whose weekly workflow carries the older checkout pin has it rewritten by `cursor-configurator` from the frozen block at its next configuration touch or change cycle, through the gate; the video factory first fixes its open Dependabot alerts, through the gate, before any build work.
+
+**If rolled back**
+- `bridge-install.py --rollback` restores 2026.11.11a. A project that calibrated to this release restores the two status lines from git, runs its next records pull request through the full gate, and re-runs the whole suite before each first push; text-form Evidence cells are refused by the older `completion-check.py` and are rewritten to name a test, which for a text-only row means the retired test is restored from git first. The agent home's `AppData` folder may stay; the older launcher does not read it.
+
+**Field acceptance**: on the first project to resume, one records-only pull request merged through the short gate with `premerge-records` printing `SHORT GATE`; one increment merged with CI's run as its only whole suite; one resume after a compaction where the hook's list is the three items; `pace-report.py` printing a round-cause line. Four weeks after the install the maintainer compares rounds per increment, hours per increment and escaped defects with weeks 42 to 45; a rise in escaped defects reopens the item that let it through.
